	'about_s1_p1' => 'Hibana College was founded in 2011. It is a welding and metal-fabrication trade school for adults changing jobs. The workshop and the office are at 27 Slipway Road, Port Aldren. Marit Solberg is principal and founder. She left shipyard fitting to teach adults who had never held a torch, and the college still takes that person as its student. The application is a one-page form. No experience is required. The day course is 26 weeks, the cohort is 12, and two instructors stay on the floor. People who need a shorter route use Evening Foundations, the TIG Short Course or Taster Day. The college teaches in this workshop only. It does not describe itself as a university, and it does not offer a qualification under another institution\'s name.',
