	'fees_s1_h' => 'Five fees',
	'fees_s1_p1' => 'All fees are in US dollars. The Six-Month Course is 26 weeks and 728 hours, with the kit included, at $9,800. Evening Foundations is 12 weeks, two evenings a week and 72 hours, at $2,400. The TIG Short Course is four Saturdays and 24 hours, at $980. Taster Day is one Saturday and six hours, at $180. Graduate Booth Hire is one 3-hour session at $45. Open Bench, on the first Saturday of each month from 10:00 to 13:00, is free. The five paid items are separate. A Taster Day fee does not come off the Six-Month Course, and an evening place is not a deposit on a day cohort. Each enrolment is paid as its own fee. The office can confirm which item a date belongs to.',
	'fees_s2_h' => 'Paying for the Six-Month Course',
	'fees_s2_p1' => 'The Six-Month Course is paid as a $500 deposit and then six monthly payments of $1,550. Those amounts add up to $9,800. The deposit is taken on day one, and it secures a booth. The kit is issued on the first morning: helmet, jacket, gloves and boots. The kit is included in the $9,800. It is not a further charge. The six monthly payments follow the deposit. Evening Foundations at $2,400, the TIG Short Course at $980, Taster Day at $180 and Graduate Booth Hire at $45 are not collected on this plan. They are single fees for those shorter enrolments. Cohort dates for the day course remain 11 January, 3 May and 6 September. The deposit is tied to day one of the cohort a student is actually joining.',
	'fees_s3_h' => 'Withdrawal',
	'fees_s3_p1' => 'The deposit is refundable up to 14 days before day one. A student who withdraws inside that window can have the $500 returned. The kit is issued on the first morning, so the refund window closes before the helmet, jacket, gloves and boots are handed out, and before the booth is taken up for the term. Questions about a withdrawal go to the office, Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 17:00, at hello@hibanacollege.example or +1 555 0142. The 14 days are counted back from day one of that student\'s cohort, not from the date of Open Bench or from the bench talk. Open Bench itself is free and has nothing to refund.',
	'fees_s4_h' => 'What the fee pays for',
