	'other_courses_alt1' => 'Close view of a TIG torch and filler rod over stainless',
	'other_courses_h1' => 'Other Courses',
	'other_courses_intro' => 'Four shorter offerings sit beside the Six-Month Course. Each has its own length, hours and fee, in US dollars.',
	'other_courses_next' => 'See the fees',
	'other_courses_s1_h' => 'Evening Foundations',
	'other_courses_s1_p1' => 'Evening Foundations is 12 weeks, on two evenings a week, for 72 hours. The fee is $2,400. The evenings are Tuesday and Thursday, 18:00 to 21:00. It is the way to study here if the day course, Monday to Thursday from 8:30 to 16:30, does not fit around other work. No experience is needed to apply. The evening course is not the Six-Month Course. It does not run to 728 hours, it is not one of the three day cohorts, and the two-week placement in month 6 belongs to the day course. A place on Tuesday and Thursday evenings does not hold a booth for 11 January, 3 May or 6 September. Someone who later wants the full course applies for that cohort in the ordinary way.',
	'other_courses_s2_h' => 'TIG Short Course',
	'other_courses_s2_p1' => 'The TIG Short Course is four Saturdays, 24 hours in all, and the fee is $980. It is a separate enrolment for people who want a short run of TIG teaching without taking 26 weeks. On the Six-Month Course, TIG is month 4, taught as TIG, Steel & Stainless: torch and filler control, with a clean stainless butt joint leaving the bench. The Saturday course is not that month, and attending it does not take the place of month 4 for a student already in a day cohort. It has no share in the two-week placement. Dates for the four Saturdays are given by the office when you ask. The day cohorts still begin only on 11 January, 3 May and 6 September. Write to hello@hibanacollege.example or call +1 555 0142 during office hours.',
	'other_courses_s3_h' => 'Taster Day',
	'other_courses_s3_p1' => 'Taster Day is one Saturday, six hours, and the fee is $180. It suits someone who wants a single taught day and is not ready to apply for 26 weeks or for the 12-week evening course. Open Bench remains the usual first visit: it is free, on the first Saturday of each month, from 10:00 to 13:00, and a visitor tries a torch under supervision. Taster Day is the paid Saturday, longer than that morning, with teaching rather than a first try only. No experience is required. Paying for the Saturday does not reserve a booth. A booth on the Six-Month Course is held by the $500 deposit on day one of a cohort, after the application and the bench talk. The office takes questions Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 17:00.',
	'other_courses_s4_h' => 'Graduate Booth Hire',
	'other_courses_s4_p1' => 'Graduate Booth Hire is one 3-hour session at $45. It is for a graduate who wants a booth in the workshop again after finishing here. The session is not a class, not a test and not a placement. It is not included in the $9,800 Six-Month Course fee, and it is not part of the kit. The kit issued on the first morning of that course is a helmet, a jacket, gloves and boots. Booth hire is only the three hours at $45. The workshop address is 27 Slipway Road, Port Aldren. Ask the office on a weekday between 9:00 and 17:00, or email hello@hibanacollege.example. Evening course hours and Open Bench occupy other parts of the week; hire is arranged so it does not cut across a cohort already in the booths.',
